<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Nagod State</h1><p class="st-meta">1344 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Nagod</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Parihar Rajput state in Baghelkhand, ruled first from Unchahara and later from Nagod, among the states of central India's Bagelkhand Agency.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parihar">Parihar</a> rulers claimed descent from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/gurjara-pratihara">Gurjara-Pratihara dynasty</a> and tradition dates their rule in the area to 1344, with an early seat at Unchahara. The capital moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagod">Nagod</a> in the 18th century.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagod">Nagod</a> was a small agricultural state between Rewa and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/panna-state">Panna</a>. It came under British protection in the early 19th century and was later administered through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghelkhand-agency">Bagelkhand Agency</a>. Little detailed history is recorded.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After independence <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagod">Nagod</a> joined <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/vindhya-pradesh">Vindhya Pradesh</a>, which merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a> in 1956. It is now in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satna-district">Satna district</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/nagod-state.jpg" alt="Nagod State" width="304" height="207"><figcaption>Image: Xufanc · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nagod_state_flag.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1344 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Nagod</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Bagheli</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Unchahara</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1646&amp;focus=nagod-state" aria-label="Nagod State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6821 1273 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Nagod State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7141 1529L7364 1601M7141 1529L7364 1602M7141 1529L7160 1530"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7160 1530h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7141 1529h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7141 1529h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1646&amp;focus=nagod-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
